{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final report — root cause, experiments, fix (Gerrit change 2359)\n\n### Root cause (proven, at source — timeout stays 30s)\nGit >=2.47 runs `git maintenance run --auto` **foreground, inside `git commit`**.\nUnder ADR 0051's store config (`gc.autoDetach=false`, `maintenance.autoDetach=false`,\n`gc.auto` unset -> git's ~6700 loose-object threshold), once a mature store crosses the\nloose-object threshold that inline maintenance performs an **O(store) repack inside the\nlock-held commit subprocess** — whose cost is charged to `event_commit_git._GIT_TIMEOUT`\n(30s). When the repack exceeds 30s the watchdog SIGKILLs git mid-`repack`, losing the write\nand risking a corrupt/half-written store. Raising 30s->120s only moves the cliff to a larger\nstore, which is exactly why the operator rejected it: the timeout is a *symptom*.\n\n### Discriminating experiments (mechanism observed at runtime, not just code-read)\n- **H: store size / foreground repack (CONFIRMED).** With a store filled past git's loose\n  threshold and `_GIT_TIMEOUT` monkeypatched small, `create_ticket` reproducibly fails with\n  `git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out` — and the *same* write **succeeds**\n  once auto-maintenance is suppressed on the commit. Direct cause->effect on the mechanism.\n- **H: network/push counted inside the commit bound (FALSIFIED).** The 30s bound wraps only\n  the `git commit` subprocess; auto-push runs after, on its own path — removing the network\n  step does not change the commit-timeout failure.\n- **H: lock contention/serialization (FALSIFIED as the >30s driver).** The single commit\n  subprocess itself exceeds 30s in isolation once the repack fires; contention is not needed\n  to reproduce. (ADR 0051 serialization is *preserved* by the fix — see below.)\n- **H: a regression made a fast path slow (FALSIFIED).** The cost is git's own inline\n  maintenance crossing a threshold on a mature store, not a rebar code regression.\n\n### Fix (RED->GREEN, landed via Gerrit; 30s + c2ba parity test untouched)\nSplit the commit from its maintenance. `_AUTOMAINT_OFF`\n(`-c gc.auto=0 -c maintenance.auto=false`) suppresses git's inline auto-maintenance on every\nlock-held store commit (making the bounded commit O(1)); `gitutil.run_auto_maintenance` then\nruns the identical `git maintenance run --auto` as an explicit **deferred** step under the\n**same write lock** on the 120s `_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT` watchdog. This keeps ADR 0051's\nserialized foreground maintenance intact while moving its cost off the tight commit bound —\n`git maintenance run --auto` is exactly what git invokes automatically, so the deferred repack\nis equivalent, just no longer charged to `_GIT_TIMEOUT`.\n\n**Surfaces covered** (every lock-held store-commit site that builds its own argv):\nevent_append `_git_commit`/`_git_commit_paths` + recovery commits\n(`_recover_from_unmerged`, `_recover_from_invalid_object`) with post-commit deferred\nmaintenance; `txn.py` claim/transition (same pattern); suppress-only on `delete.py`,\n`compact_plan.py`, `compact.py` (ticket-compact-all backfill) and `fsck_repair.py`\n(a3-remediation batches) — the maintenance/repair paths where an unserialized off-lock repack\nis disallowed, so their loose objects are repacked by the next LOCKED write's deferred\nmaintenance.\n\n### Validation\n- RED confirmed (write fails \"git timed out\"), GREEN confirmed after fix, in\n  `tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py`.\n- c2ba parity test (pins `_GIT_TIMEOUT=30`) stays green.\n- Focused suites green on touched surfaces: store batch/delete/index-reset/unmerged/gitutil,\n  txn/claim/lifecycle, import_batch_resume, compact (52), fsck repair (66+2).\n- `make lint` (ruff + complexity baseline) + `make typecheck` clean.\n- `review-plan` verdict: **PASS** (0 blocking).\n\n### Honest caveat (kept per skill)\nThis fixes the failure **class** — a foreground O(store) repack charged to a bounded,\nlock-held commit on a **mature** store. The specific historical F07 run was against a\n**fresh** temp store (few objects, below the ~6700 threshold), so foreground maintenance\nlikely does not explain *that individual node* — but it is the mechanism behind the class the\nAC asks to fix. If a fresh-store timeout recurs, it needs a separate investigation (a distinct\ncause), and I'd recommend a follow-up ticket linked `discovered_from` this one.\n\n### Landing status\nGerrit change: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2359\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` (review-bot) and `Verified +1` (CI full suite, rebased onto current\nmain). Ticket will be closed only after both votes are green AND the change merges, with\n`--class=regression --caused-by=c2ba-98bf-ca2d-481a`. NOT closing now."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787965347822706001,"uuid":"4764a2af-58c1-43ad-943c-296f08143144"}